{
  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) achieves 0.485 acc, and config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) improves to 0.527, confirming that adding image helps. However, the multiprofile axis (with aggregation) remains entirely untested. Question: Does using multiple profiles with avgpool aggregation improve over the single-profile baseline for the same RNA encoder (pca_n2000)? This directly compares to config_001, changing only the profile/aggregation setting while holding model setting and RNA encoder fixed. Why this is the best next experiment: The multiprofile decision is the most consequential unexplored axis—if it provides a meaningful gain in the simpler rna_only setting, it is very likely to compound in multimodal configurations (configs 018–051), and we should prioritize those; if it does not help, we can safely focus remaining budget on singleprofile configurations and other axes (RNA encoder, image encoder, fusion). Testing this in rna_only isolates the aggregation effect without the confound of multimodal fusion, making the result maximally interpretable under the limited budget."
}

